The native adaptation computes division by X-x, proves its root-factor
identity and actual principal evaluation kernel, constructs checked ring
map kernels and evaluation naturality, and evaluates the actual quadratic
coordinate algebra using its proved monic-quadratic quotient correspondence.
It proves the actual XY point ideal equals the evaluation kernel, constructs
the quotient setoid ring, and supplies two checked inverse ring maps via
the actual constant section. The quotient relation is separately proved to
mean that the difference is an actual XYIdeal member.

This is a constructive setoid adaptation of quotientXYIdealEquiv. It does
not import Lean proof objects or the full Mathlib quotient, module, algebra
and typeclass infrastructure. Quotient module dimensions, nonsingular ideal
inverse/addition identities, fractional ideals, class groups, point group
laws and the general FLT proof remain separate open obligations.
